        "uri": "https://github.com/traefik/traefik/pull/10388",
        "locator": "description (part 2)",
        "excerpt": "\"starting up\", which is a different state than \"critical\", but not yet ready for traffic. The existing build sends traffic immediately to \"warning\" upstreams, which causes 5XX errors for our use case.\n\nWith this config, users can choose what health status to allow based on the available statuses that Consul supports as their organization requires.\n\n### More\n\n- [X] Added/updated tests\n- [X] Added/updated documentation\n\n### Additional Notes\n\nQuestion: will I need to add additional logic to properly handle the …",
